# Editor
.idea/
# VS Code settings stay ignored EXCEPT the committed workspace settings:
# `typescript.tsdk` is what makes the editor resolve `@types/node` through the
# checkout's own TypeScript instead of whichever one VS Code bundled (see
# .vscode/settings.json). A blanket `.vscode/` would silently drop it.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

